<p>Per ESPN, he's also the first receiver since 1966 with at least 850 yards and 8 touchdowns through seven games. This comes after a 2025 season in which he led the league with 1,793 receiving yards and was named Offensive Player of the Year. "He's unguardable," Seahawks safety Nick Emmanwori said after the Chiefs game.</p>
<h2>The Combine He Didn't Finish</h2>
<p>Smith-Njigba arrived at the 2023 combine with questions. A hamstring injury had limited him to three games in his final season at Ohio State, and he chose not to run the 40 in Indianapolis, saying he hadn't had enough reps at it yet. He did run the agility drills, and those numbers were special.</p>
