</table></div>
<p>A 4.48 is fast but not rare for a first-round receiver, and Seattle took him 20th overall in 2023 as the first receiver off the board. The agility times were the outliers. A sub-4.0 shuttle from a wide receiver is uncommon, and pairing it with a 6.57 three-cone put him in rare company for change of direction.</p>
